1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,554
Today's video is all about emotions—joy, sadness, anger. You won’t want to miss it, or you might just get mad!

2
00:00:10,554 --> 00:00:18,576
At some point in the video, a question will appear in Japanese. If you catch it, leave a comment!

3
00:00:19,196 --> 00:00:22,656
Scene 1: Losing a Favorite Umbrella and What to Do

4
00:00:23,015 --> 00:00:26,215
Oh no, what should I do?

5
00:00:26,237 --> 00:00:28,478
What happened?

6
00:00:28,502 --> 00:00:32,553
I lost my favorite umbrella.

7
00:00:32,577 --> 00:00:36,177
Oh, you mean the blue one?

8
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:39,400
Yes, that one.

9
00:00:39,423 --> 00:00:42,028
Where did you lose it?

10
00:00:42,051 --> 00:00:45,107
Probably on the train.

11
00:00:45,130 --> 00:00:48,663
Did you call the train company?

12
00:00:48,686 --> 00:00:51,863
No, not yet.

13
00:00:51,887 --> 00:00:55,464
You should call them right away.

14
00:00:55,487 --> 00:00:59,061
But I don’t think they’ll find it.

15
00:00:59,084 --> 00:01:02,451
You never know—they might!

16
00:01:02,474 --> 00:01:06,330
That umbrella meant a lot to me.

17
00:01:06,353 --> 00:01:08,828
Where did you buy it?

18
00:01:08,852 --> 00:01:13,335
My sister gave it to me for my birthday last year.

19
00:01:13,359 --> 00:01:16,218
That’s really sad.

20
00:01:16,241 --> 00:01:19,857
Yeah, I’m really shocked.

21
00:01:19,881 --> 00:01:23,147
Don’t give up—let’s call them.

22
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:26,857
I don’t know the number.

23
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:30,520
I’ll look it up on my phone right now.

24
00:01:30,544 --> 00:01:32,211
Thank you.

25
00:01:32,234 --> 00:01:36,167
Oh, here’s the number!

26
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:37,757
Really?

27
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:41,079
Yes, call this number.

28
00:01:41,103 --> 00:01:44,169
I’m a little nervous.

29
00:01:44,192 --> 00:01:48,088
It’s okay, it’s okay!

30
00:01:48,111 --> 00:01:51,925
What if it’s not there?

31
00:01:51,949 --> 00:01:56,982
If it’s not, we’ll go buy a new umbrella together.

32
00:01:57,006 --> 00:02:01,406
And I’ll get you a really cute one!

33
00:02:01,429 --> 00:02:03,401
Really?

34
00:02:03,424 --> 00:02:07,258
Yeah, so cheer up!

35
00:02:07,281 --> 00:02:08,922
Thank you.

36
00:02:08,945 --> 00:02:11,800
I feel a little better now.

37
00:02:11,823 --> 00:02:15,423
Alright, let’s call them first.

38
00:02:15,446 --> 00:02:18,646
Okay, I’ll give them a call.

39
00:02:18,669 --> 00:02:25,774
You can review today’s video with the link in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

40
00:02:25,774 --> 00:02:28,774
Scene 2: Surprise Reunion

41
00:02:28,774 --> 00:02:33,341
Wait… is that Ken?

42
00:02:33,364 --> 00:02:35,062
Huh?

43
00:02:35,085 --> 00:02:38,732
Oh, yeah, it’s me.

44
00:02:38,756 --> 00:02:42,289
It’s me—Hana!

45
00:02:42,312 --> 00:02:46,081
What?! Hana?!

46
00:02:46,105 --> 00:02:50,777
Yeah, it’s been so long!

47
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:53,266
I can’t believe it!

48
00:02:53,289 --> 00:02:56,549
It really is you, Hana!

49
00:02:56,572 --> 00:03:02,139
Yep, it’s been about ten years!

50
00:03:02,162 --> 00:03:05,729
What are you doing here?

51
00:03:05,752 --> 00:03:09,352
I came here to do some shopping.

52
00:03:09,375 --> 00:03:14,142
Oh, I work here.

53
00:03:14,165 --> 00:03:18,809
Wait, do you work around here?

54
00:03:18,832 --> 00:03:22,638
Yes, I do. Right over there in that office.

55
00:03:22,662 --> 00:03:28,064
Wow, you haven’t changed a bit!

56
00:03:28,088 --> 00:03:32,854
Well, I’ve put on a little weight.

57
00:03:32,877 --> 00:03:37,011
You never know—they might!

58
00:03:37,034 --> 00:03:41,967
So, Hana, what do you do now?

59
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:45,726
I’m an English teacher.

60
00:03:45,749 --> 00:03:49,720
An English teacher? Really?

61
00:03:49,743 --> 00:03:52,176
That’s amazing!

62
00:03:52,199 --> 00:03:54,133
Thank you.

63
00:03:54,156 --> 00:03:58,989
It’s busy every day, but I love it.

64
00:03:59,012 --> 00:04:03,428
I’m so happy we got to meet today.

65
00:04:03,452 --> 00:04:09,052
I’m really surprised—and happy too!

66
00:04:09,075 --> 00:04:12,608
Do you have some time now?

67
00:04:12,631 --> 00:04:17,517
Yeah, I’ve got about an hour.

68
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:22,217
Then how about grabbing tea at a café nearby?

69
00:04:22,241 --> 00:04:25,443
Sounds great. Let’s go!

70
00:04:25,466 --> 00:04:29,433
There’s a place with delicious cake!

71
00:04:29,456 --> 00:04:32,625
Ooh, I can’t wait!

72
00:04:32,648 --> 00:04:35,882
We’ve got so much to catch up on!

73
00:04:35,905 --> 00:04:40,638
Yeah, I’ve got a lot to tell you too.

74
00:04:40,661 --> 00:04:43,833
Alright, let’s head out.

75
00:04:43,856 --> 00:04:46,689
Yeah, let’s go!

76
00:04:46,712 --> 00:04:52,865
Let me know if you could understand that in the comments!

77
00:04:52,865 --> 00:04:55,865
Scene 3: Preparing for Our Okinawa Trip

78
00:04:55,865 --> 00:05:00,563
Our Okinawa trip starts tomorrow—can you believe it?

79
00:05:00,587 --> 00:05:04,393
I know! I’m so excited!

80
00:05:04,416 --> 00:05:08,053
Have you finished packing yet?

81
00:05:08,077 --> 00:05:11,521
No, not yet.

82
00:05:11,544 --> 00:05:15,011
You’d better hurry up and pack!

83
00:05:15,034 --> 00:05:18,110
How many outfits should I bring?

84
00:05:18,133 --> 00:05:23,013
Okinawa’s warm, so T-shirts would be perfect.

85
00:05:23,036 --> 00:05:24,836
Got it.

86
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:27,110
I’ll bring plenty.

87
00:05:27,133 --> 00:05:31,310
I can’t wait to swim in the ocean!

88
00:05:31,333 --> 00:05:35,967
Yeah, I want to see the beautiful sea too.

89
00:05:35,990 --> 00:05:38,441
Did you bring your camera?

90
00:05:38,464 --> 00:05:41,232
Of course I did!

91
00:05:41,255 --> 00:05:44,272
Let’s take lots of photos!

92
00:05:44,296 --> 00:05:48,663
Yeah! And let’s snap some of the delicious food too.

93
00:05:48,686 --> 00:05:52,619
Oh! I want to try Okinawa soba.

94
00:05:52,642 --> 00:05:54,710
That sounds great!

95
00:05:54,733 --> 00:05:57,103
I want to try it too.

96
00:05:57,127 --> 00:06:00,093
Where’s the guidebook?

97
00:06:00,116 --> 00:06:02,319
Right here!

98
00:06:02,343 --> 00:06:05,545
Where should we go tomorrow night?

99
00:06:05,568 --> 00:06:08,785
How about that restaurant by the sea?

100
00:06:08,809 --> 00:06:10,947
That sounds lovely!

101
00:06:10,970 --> 00:06:13,174
Let’s go there.

102
00:06:13,198 --> 00:06:15,409
What’s the weather going to be like?

103
00:06:15,432 --> 00:06:17,883
It’s supposed to be sunny tomorrow!

104
00:06:17,906 --> 00:06:19,747
That’s great!

105
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:22,742
This is going to be the best trip ever!

106
00:06:22,766 --> 00:06:26,766
Hehe, yeah. Let’s turn in early tonight.

107
00:06:26,789 --> 00:06:30,995
But I might be too excited to sleep.

108
00:06:31,018 --> 00:06:34,351
Hehe, you sound like a kid.

109
00:06:34,374 --> 00:06:37,141
True, though.

110
00:06:37,164 --> 00:06:40,002
But I’m really looking forward to it.

111
00:06:40,025 --> 00:06:44,226
Set an alarm so we don’t oversleep.

112
00:06:44,250 --> 00:06:47,383
Already did.

113
00:06:47,406 --> 00:06:51,851
Alright, we’ve got an early start tomorrow, but let’s do our best!

114
00:06:51,874 --> 00:06:54,909
Yeah! Let’s have a great time.

115
00:06:54,933 --> 00:06:57,933
Scene 4: Handling a Lost Wallet

116
00:06:57,933 --> 00:07:00,866
Oh no, what should I do?

117
00:07:00,889 --> 00:07:03,556
My wallet’s gone!

118
00:07:03,579 --> 00:07:05,459
What?

119
00:07:05,482 --> 00:07:07,849
Really?

120
00:07:07,872 --> 00:07:11,117
Did you check your bag?

121
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:16,607
Yeah, I checked everywhere. It’s not here.

122
00:07:16,630 --> 00:07:20,563
Do you remember where you might’ve lost it?

123
00:07:20,586 --> 00:07:22,919
I don’t know.

124
00:07:22,942 --> 00:07:26,809
I had it when I was shopping earlier.

125
00:07:26,832 --> 00:07:29,965
Let’s go to the police box.

126
00:07:29,988 --> 00:07:34,887
It’s got all my money and cards in it!

127
00:07:34,911 --> 00:07:37,044
Stay calm.

128
00:07:37,067 --> 00:07:39,647
It’ll be okay.

129
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:43,270
Do you really think we’ll find it?

130
00:07:43,293 --> 00:07:48,293
Japanese police are really helpful—it’s probably there.

131
00:07:48,317 --> 00:07:50,987
There’s a police box over there.

132
00:07:51,010 --> 00:07:52,777
Let’s go.

133
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:57,214
Excuse me, has anyone turned in a wallet?

134
00:07:57,237 --> 00:08:00,638
It’s a black leather wallet.

135
00:08:00,662 --> 00:08:04,895
Oh, the officer went to the back.

136
00:08:04,918 --> 00:08:08,985
My heart’s racing.

137
00:08:09,008 --> 00:08:11,699
Oh, they’re bringing something out.

138
00:08:11,723 --> 00:08:15,456
That’s my wallet!

139
00:08:15,479 --> 00:08:18,012
Really?

140
00:08:18,035 --> 00:08:20,402
That’s great!

141
00:08:20,426 --> 00:08:23,833
Yes, that’s definitely it.

142
00:08:23,857 --> 00:08:27,065
Check inside to make sure everything’s there.

143
00:08:27,088 --> 00:08:30,755
All the money and cards are here!

144
00:08:30,779 --> 00:08:33,755
Thank goodness.

145
00:08:33,779 --> 00:08:36,870
I’m so relieved.

146
00:08:36,893 --> 00:08:41,096
Yeah, what a weight off my chest.

147
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:44,686
We should thank the person who turned it in.

148
00:08:44,709 --> 00:08:50,276
Yeah, I want to say thank you to whoever was so kind.

149
00:08:50,299 --> 00:08:54,866
Heh, just don’t lose it again, okay?

150
00:08:54,889 --> 00:08:59,228
Hehe, I’ll be more careful from now on.

151
00:08:59,251 --> 00:09:03,710
Well, now that we’re relieved, I’m actually hungry.

152
00:09:03,733 --> 00:09:09,106
You’re right. Let me treat you to a nice meal.

153
00:09:09,130 --> 00:09:11,976
Really? Are you sure?

154
00:09:11,999 --> 00:09:13,966
That’d be great!

155
00:09:13,989 --> 00:09:18,794
Of course! Thanks for sticking with me through this.

156
00:09:18,817 --> 00:09:22,384
No problem. Let’s go!

157
00:09:22,407 --> 00:09:25,407
Scene 5: Unveiling the Latest Smartphone Features

158
00:09:25,407 --> 00:09:30,541
Check this out—I just got a new phone!

159
00:09:30,564 --> 00:09:35,098
Wow, that’s the latest model, isn’t it?

160
00:09:35,121 --> 00:09:39,728
Yep, it just came out yesterday.

161
00:09:39,751 --> 00:09:44,406
Lucky you! I’m so jealous.

162
00:09:44,430 --> 00:09:47,696
The screen is gorgeous.

163
00:09:47,719 --> 00:09:52,592
It really is! And it’s super fast too.

164
00:09:52,616 --> 00:09:56,290
The camera is amazing as well.

165
00:09:56,313 --> 00:10:00,980
My phone’s so old—I’m jealous!

166
00:10:01,003 --> 00:10:04,892
Want me to take a photo for you?

167
00:10:04,916 --> 00:10:06,565
Sure, go ahead!

168
00:10:06,589 --> 00:10:10,022
Alright, say cheese!

169
00:10:10,045 --> 00:10:15,078
Whoa, my skin looks flawless in this!

170
00:10:15,102 --> 00:10:20,268
Hehe, it even brightens up dark places.

171
00:10:20,291 --> 00:10:24,758
Ugh, I really want one now.

172
00:10:24,781 --> 00:10:28,065
It was a bit pricey, though.

173
00:10:28,088 --> 00:10:30,259
How much was it?

174
00:10:30,282 --> 00:10:32,923
150,000 yen.

175
00:10:32,947 --> 00:10:37,180
150,000 yen?! That’s expensive!

176
00:10:37,203 --> 00:10:43,236
But I use it every day, so it’s worth it.

177
00:10:43,259 --> 00:10:46,259
I’ll stick with my current phone for two more years.

178
00:10:46,282 --> 00:10:50,449
Might as well use it until it breaks.

179
00:10:50,472 --> 00:10:55,251
But now that I’ve seen yours, I kind of want one too.

180
00:10:55,275 --> 00:10:58,875
Why not buy one with your bonus next month?

181
00:10:58,898 --> 00:11:03,075
I’m planning to use my bonus for a trip.

182
00:11:03,099 --> 00:11:08,232
Then let’s take tons of photos with my phone during your trip!

183
00:11:08,255 --> 00:11:11,230
That’s a great idea!

184
00:11:11,253 --> 00:11:16,053
I’ll give you lots of beautiful photos as a gift.

185
00:11:16,076 --> 00:11:17,774
Thank you.

186
00:11:17,798 --> 00:11:19,808
I can’t wait!

187
00:11:19,832 --> 00:11:23,521
But seriously, it’s so convenient.

188
00:11:23,544 --> 00:11:27,833
Ugh, I’m jealous again.

189
00:11:27,856 --> 00:11:32,471
Don’t say that—come try it out at the café now!

190
00:11:32,495 --> 00:11:36,136
Really? I’d love to touch it!

191
00:11:36,159 --> 00:11:38,559
Here, go ahead!

192
00:11:38,583 --> 00:11:42,316
Thanks! I’m so happy!

193
00:11:42,339 --> 00:11:45,339
Scene 6: The Moment of Truth – Exam Results

194
00:11:45,339 --> 00:11:50,375
Oh, the results site just opened!

195
00:11:50,399 --> 00:11:52,537
Really?

196
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:55,173
I’m so nervous!

197
00:11:55,197 --> 00:11:58,764
Can you look up my number?

198
00:11:58,787 --> 00:12:03,396
Sure, what’s your number?

199
00:12:03,419 --> 00:12:06,673
10045.

200
00:12:06,696 --> 00:12:08,395
Is it there?

201
00:12:08,419 --> 00:12:11,110
Yes, I found it!

202
00:12:11,133 --> 00:12:12,867
It’s right here.

203
00:12:12,890 --> 00:12:15,423
Wait, really?

204
00:12:15,446 --> 00:12:17,303
Really?

205
00:12:17,326 --> 00:12:21,060
Yep, 10045.

206
00:12:21,083 --> 00:12:23,616
Congratulations, you passed!

207
00:12:23,639 --> 00:12:28,075
Yes! I’m so happy!

208
00:12:28,098 --> 00:12:29,948
I can’t believe it!

209
00:12:29,972 --> 00:12:32,944
That was really great, wasn't it?

210
00:12:32,968 --> 00:12:37,001
Well, you studied so hard every day.

211
00:12:37,024 --> 00:12:41,433
Yeah, I pushed myself late into the night every day.

212
00:12:41,456 --> 00:12:44,894
Let's celebrate tonight!

213
00:12:44,917 --> 00:12:46,752
That sounds great!

214
00:12:46,775 --> 00:12:49,842
Let's go eat something delicious.

215
00:12:49,865 --> 00:12:52,198
What do you feel like eating?

216
00:12:52,221 --> 00:12:55,188
I'm craving sushi.

217
00:12:55,211 --> 00:12:57,820
Would you like to splurge on some high-end sushi?

218
00:12:57,843 --> 00:13:00,735
Absolutely!

219
00:13:00,759 --> 00:13:03,925
Tonight's on me.

220
00:13:03,948 --> 00:13:06,915
Wait, are you sure?

221
00:13:06,938 --> 00:13:08,706
Thank you.

222
00:13:08,729 --> 00:13:12,263
It's a celebration of your hard work.

223
00:13:12,286 --> 00:13:14,452
That’d be great!

224
00:13:14,475 --> 00:13:18,875
Oh, by the way, did you get your results yet?

225
00:13:18,898 --> 00:13:21,565
Oh, I completely forgot!

226
00:13:21,589 --> 00:13:26,222
My number is 10050.

227
00:13:26,245 --> 00:13:28,978
Just a moment, please.

228
00:13:29,001 --> 00:13:30,835
Let me check.

229
00:13:30,857 --> 00:13:32,391
How's it looking?

230
00:13:32,414 --> 00:13:33,947
Is it there?

231
00:13:33,970 --> 00:13:42,403
Uh... 10048, 10049... Oh, there it is!

232
00:13:42,426 --> 00:13:45,393
Number 10050.

233
00:13:45,416 --> 00:13:48,483
Wait, you found it?

234
00:13:48,506 --> 00:13:52,120
Yes, you passed!

235
00:13:52,143 --> 00:13:54,110
Congratulations!

236
00:13:54,133 --> 00:13:56,100
We did it!

237
00:13:56,123 --> 00:13:58,556
I passed too!

238
00:13:58,579 --> 00:14:01,312
That's amazing!

239
00:14:01,335 --> 00:14:05,349
I'm so happy we both passed.

240
00:14:05,373 --> 00:14:06,982
Me too.

241
00:14:07,006 --> 00:14:09,439
This feels incredible.

242
00:14:09,462 --> 00:14:14,462
Alright, let's book a table at that amazing sushi place right now.

243
00:14:14,485 --> 00:14:17,958
Yes, I'll call them right away.

244
00:14:17,981 --> 00:14:20,981
Scene 7: The Disappointment of Missing Out on Live Concert Tickets

245
00:14:20,981 --> 00:14:25,581
The concert ticket results are in.

246
00:14:25,604 --> 00:14:27,404
How did it go?

247
00:14:27,427 --> 00:14:29,404
Did you get them?

248
00:14:29,428 --> 00:14:32,325
Ugh, no luck.

249
00:14:32,349 --> 00:14:34,282
I didn't get them.

250
00:14:34,305 --> 00:14:38,505
Wow, that's really disappointing.

251
00:14:38,528 --> 00:14:40,227
Yeah...

252
00:14:40,250 --> 00:14:44,817
I was so looking forward to it. I'm really bummed.

253
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:47,685
I'm sorry to hear that.

254
00:14:47,709 --> 00:14:52,109
We practiced so many of their new songs.

255
00:14:52,132 --> 00:14:54,227
Me too.

256
00:14:54,250 --> 00:14:57,017
I listened to them every day.

257
00:14:57,040 --> 00:15:01,073
Why didn't we get the tickets?

258
00:15:01,096 --> 00:15:05,794
This band is insanely popular.

259
00:15:05,818 --> 00:15:09,691
Getting tickets is nearly impossible.

260
00:15:09,714 --> 00:15:15,133
I don't want to give up, but there are no tickets left.

261
00:15:15,156 --> 00:15:18,037
What about the concert on a different day?

262
00:15:18,061 --> 00:15:23,228
I can't go on other days—I have work.

263
00:15:23,251 --> 00:15:25,217
I see.

264
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:28,574
That's really too bad.

265
00:15:28,597 --> 00:15:33,830
Ugh, I don’t feel like doing anything today.

266
00:15:33,853 --> 00:15:35,820
Cheer up!

267
00:15:35,843 --> 00:15:41,176
But my plans I was looking forward to got canceled.

268
00:15:41,199 --> 00:15:46,081
How about going to karaoke tonight then?

269
00:15:46,105 --> 00:15:48,350
Karaoke?

270
00:15:48,373 --> 00:15:50,024
Yeah...

271
00:15:50,047 --> 00:15:53,681
Let’s sing a ton of this band’s songs.

272
00:15:53,704 --> 00:15:56,674
That’s a great idea!

273
00:15:56,698 --> 00:16:00,065
And let’s eat lots of good food too.

274
00:16:00,088 --> 00:16:01,821
Thank you.

275
00:16:01,844 --> 00:16:04,677
I feel a little better now.

276
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:08,434
How about the karaoke place near the station?

277
00:16:08,457 --> 00:16:11,990
That place has great big rooms, doesn’t it?

278
00:16:12,013 --> 00:16:15,313
Alright, I’ll make a reservation now.

279
00:16:15,336 --> 00:16:17,213
Yes, please do.

280
00:16:17,237 --> 00:16:21,870
Let’s sing our hearts out and forget how bummed we are.

281
00:16:21,893 --> 00:16:23,427
Me too.

282
00:16:23,449 --> 00:16:25,853
I’ll sing my lungs out!

283
00:16:25,877 --> 00:16:27,976
Nice.

284
00:16:27,999 --> 00:16:30,966
Let’s meet at the station then.

285
00:16:30,989 --> 00:16:32,428
Yeah...

286
00:16:32,452 --> 00:16:34,819
See you later.

287
00:16:34,841 --> 00:16:37,841
Scene 8: Easing Pre-Interview Jitters

288
00:16:37,841 --> 00:16:40,975
Oh no, what should I do?

289
00:16:40,998 --> 00:16:44,372
I’m so nervous.

290
00:16:44,395 --> 00:16:46,834
It’s okay, you’ll be fine.

291
00:16:46,858 --> 00:16:48,940
Stay calm.

292
00:16:48,963 --> 00:16:52,730
My hands are shaking a little.

293
00:16:52,753 --> 00:16:56,167
Take a deep breath.

294
00:16:56,190 --> 00:17:02,272
Breathe in… and out…

295
00:17:02,295 --> 00:17:07,368
*Inhales*… *Exhales*…

296
00:17:07,392 --> 00:17:09,792
I feel a little better now.

297
00:17:09,815 --> 00:17:13,651
What time does your interview start?

298
00:17:13,674 --> 00:17:17,674
In fifteen minutes.

299
00:17:17,697 --> 00:17:20,897
We still have time.

300
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:25,720
I’m worried I won’t answer the questions well.

301
00:17:25,743 --> 00:17:29,435
Want to practice a little together?

302
00:17:29,459 --> 00:17:31,869
Sure, go ahead!

303
00:17:31,893 --> 00:17:35,426
Why do you want to work at this café?

304
00:17:35,449 --> 00:17:40,849
Because I love this café’s coffee and cakes.

305
00:17:40,872 --> 00:17:43,124
That sounds great!

306
00:17:43,148 --> 00:17:47,953
And the staff here is so nice.

307
00:17:47,976 --> 00:17:49,910
Me too.

308
00:17:49,933 --> 00:17:54,799
Everyone’s always smiling.

309
00:17:54,822 --> 00:17:58,227
That’s a great answer!

310
00:17:58,250 --> 00:18:00,817
Be confident.

311
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,573
Thank you.

312
00:18:02,596 --> 00:18:06,996
How many days a week can you work?

313
00:18:07,019 --> 00:18:10,653
I can work three days a week.

314
00:18:10,676 --> 00:18:14,163
Weekends are fine too.

315
00:18:14,186 --> 00:18:19,753
They’ll be happy to hear that.

316
00:18:19,776 --> 00:18:22,109
You think so?

317
00:18:22,132 --> 00:18:27,999
Yeah, weekend staff are super important.

318
00:18:28,022 --> 00:18:31,222
I feel a little more at ease now.

319
00:18:31,245 --> 00:18:35,081
You’ve got this, no doubt.

320
00:18:35,104 --> 00:18:39,183
I’m glad you came with me.

321
00:18:39,206 --> 00:18:43,140
Of course—I’m your friend!

322
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:46,563
Yeah. I’ll do my best.

323
00:18:46,586 --> 00:18:51,989
I’ll be waiting here when you’re done.

324
00:18:52,013 --> 00:18:54,981
Okay, I’ll let you know when it’s over.

325
00:18:55,004 --> 00:18:57,222
Good luck!

326
00:18:57,246 --> 00:18:59,337
I'm rooting for you.

327
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:02,975
I'm off.

328
00:19:02,999 --> 00:19:05,999
Scene 9: Noticing a Backwards T-Shirt

329
00:19:05,999 --> 00:19:10,080
Today's café is so peaceful and nice, isn't it?

330
00:19:10,103 --> 00:19:11,970
Me too.

331
00:19:11,993 --> 00:19:15,050
The coffee is delicious too.

332
00:19:15,073 --> 00:19:20,673
Um, this is a little awkward to say...

333
00:19:20,696 --> 00:19:22,229
What is it?

334
00:19:22,252 --> 00:19:24,485
Is something wrong?

335
00:19:24,508 --> 00:19:29,708
Your T-shirt... is it on backwards?

336
00:19:29,731 --> 00:19:31,430
Huh?

337
00:19:31,454 --> 00:19:33,587
What do you mean?

338
00:19:33,610 --> 00:19:36,943
It's inside out. The front and back are reversed.

339
00:19:36,966 --> 00:19:39,009
The tag is showing.

340
00:19:39,033 --> 00:19:42,366
Oh no, you're kidding!

341
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:44,356
Really?

342
00:19:44,379 --> 00:19:45,512
Yeah...

343
00:19:45,535 --> 00:19:50,335
The tag that should be at the back of your neck is in the front.

344
00:19:50,358 --> 00:19:54,217
Oh wow, you're right. How embarrassing!

345
00:19:54,241 --> 00:19:56,207
Heh heh heh.

346
00:19:56,230 --> 00:19:58,831
How long has it been like that?

347
00:19:58,854 --> 00:20:03,033
It's been like this all morning.

348
00:20:03,057 --> 00:20:05,535
You took the train, right?

349
00:20:05,558 --> 00:20:07,391
Yeah...

350
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:10,153
I was on a packed train.

351
00:20:10,176 --> 00:20:13,343
You went to a convenience store too, didn't you?

352
00:20:13,366 --> 00:20:15,138
Yeah...

353
00:20:15,161 --> 00:20:18,161
I talked to the store clerk.

354
00:20:18,184 --> 00:20:22,022
No one told you?

355
00:20:22,046 --> 00:20:26,779
Ah, that's why everyone was looking at me!

356
00:20:26,802 --> 00:20:28,935
Heh heh.

357
00:20:28,958 --> 00:20:31,125
This is so embarrassing.

358
00:20:31,148 --> 00:20:35,194
My face is burning up.

359
00:20:35,217 --> 00:20:39,475
You should go to the restroom and fix it quickly.

360
00:20:39,499 --> 00:20:41,143
Yeah...

361
00:20:41,166 --> 00:20:43,099
I'll go right now.

362
00:20:43,122 --> 00:20:46,656
Leave your bag here.

363
00:20:46,679 --> 00:20:48,445
I'll keep an eye on it.

364
00:20:48,468 --> 00:20:50,083
Thank you.

365
00:20:50,107 --> 00:20:52,440
I'll run and be back.

366
00:20:52,463 --> 00:20:55,348
Be careful.

367
00:20:55,371 --> 00:20:59,385
This has been such an embarrassing day.

368
00:20:59,409 --> 00:21:01,942
It’s okay, you’ll be fine.

369
00:21:01,965 --> 00:21:04,639
No one even noticed.

370
00:21:04,663 --> 00:21:07,533
I hope so.

371
00:21:07,556 --> 00:21:11,690
Go ahead and come back feeling refreshed.

372
00:21:11,712 --> 00:21:13,487
Yeah...

373
00:21:13,511 --> 00:21:15,401
I'll be right back.

374
00:21:15,425 --> 00:21:17,558
Heh heh.

375
00:21:17,581 --> 00:21:20,314
No rush.

376
00:21:20,337 --> 00:21:23,337
Scene 10: How to Apologize for Being Late

377
00:21:23,337 --> 00:21:26,304
You're really late.

378
00:21:26,327 --> 00:21:30,127
It's been thirty minutes already.

379
00:21:30,150 --> 00:21:34,083
I'm so sorry for being late.

380
00:21:34,106 --> 00:21:37,706
Why didn't you contact me?

381
00:21:37,729 --> 00:21:42,199
My phone died.

382
00:21:42,223 --> 00:21:47,389
Even if your phone died, you could have called from a payphone.

383
00:21:47,412 --> 00:21:52,146
I'm sorry. I didn't think of that.

384
00:21:52,169 --> 00:21:56,902
I've been worried sick here the whole time.

385
00:21:56,925 --> 00:22:00,860
I'm truly sorry.

386
00:22:00,883 --> 00:22:03,979
You're always late, aren't you?

387
00:22:04,002 --> 00:22:06,493
Same as last week.

388
00:22:06,517 --> 00:22:10,756
Yes, I'm really sorry about that.

389
00:22:10,780 --> 00:22:15,648
Punctuality is very important, you know.

390
00:22:15,671 --> 00:22:18,838
Yes, I understand.

391
00:22:18,861 --> 00:22:23,094
I feel like you don’t value my time.

392
00:22:23,117 --> 00:22:26,084
That’s not true.

393
00:22:26,107 --> 00:22:28,960
I truly regret it.

394
00:22:28,983 --> 00:22:34,723
The movie I was looking forward to has already started.

395
00:22:34,746 --> 00:22:35,913
Huh?

396
00:22:35,936 --> 00:22:38,184
Really?

397
00:22:38,208 --> 00:22:42,808
Yeah, we missed the first fifteen minutes.

398
00:22:42,831 --> 00:22:46,901
Oh, I’m really sorry about that.

399
00:22:46,924 --> 00:22:50,059
Why are you always late?

400
00:22:50,083 --> 00:22:54,771
I overslept this morning.

401
00:22:54,795 --> 00:22:58,528
You should use multiple alarms.

402
00:22:58,551 --> 00:23:01,985
Yes, I’ll do that starting today.

403
00:23:02,009 --> 00:23:07,009
I don’t want to be angry, but I’m really disappointed.

404
00:23:07,032 --> 00:23:09,504
Please forgive me.

405
00:23:09,527 --> 00:23:12,897
I’ll buy the tickets next time.

406
00:23:12,920 --> 00:23:15,977
It’s not about the money.

407
00:23:16,001 --> 00:23:20,018
You’re right—it’s about respect.

408
00:23:20,041 --> 00:23:24,246
You must never be late again.

409
00:23:24,269 --> 00:23:27,203
Yes, I promise.

410
00:23:27,226 --> 00:23:29,592
I won’t be late again.

411
00:23:29,615 --> 00:23:31,649
Got it.

412
00:23:31,672 --> 00:23:34,105
I’ll let it slide this time.

413
00:23:34,128 --> 00:23:36,132
Thank you.

414
00:23:36,155 --> 00:23:38,922
Let’s hurry to the theater.

415
00:23:38,945 --> 00:23:41,911
Yes, let’s rush!